## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Support inclusive start_date/end_date, at most 31 inclusive days, grouping by date/zone_name, sort by date/zone_name/volume, page and per_page up to 10000 (default 1000).
- [ ] Do not accept volume as a grouping: it is a measure/sort field despite the schema enum. Encode multiple groupings and sort terms as comma-separated strings.
- [ ] Decode rows as arrays of cells aligned with headers, not the schema's flat scalar array; retain query.account_id/dates/sort/groupings/page/per_page and returned pagination.
- [ ] Return {:ok, {DnsAnalytics.Result.t(), pagination}}; the deliberate list_all helper concatenates compatible rows while retaining first-page headers/query as documented provenance, without inventing aggregate pagination.
- [ ] Preserve returned zero-based metadata from the stale example without changing the documented one-based request convention; test no repeated-page loops and header/query-filter mismatch errors during enumeration.
- [ ] The explicit list_page surface returns {:ok, {typed_items, pagination}} for one page, with the documented string-keyed metadata. The list/query convenience alias returns the identical result without enumerating. The explicit list_all helper starts at page 1, rejects :page, preserves filters/sort/per_page/order and returns an error rather than success-shaped partial data if any page fails. Applied-service names use the corresponding _applied suffix; analytics retains its typed tabular payload.
